{
  "title": "Python Question Bank & Mastery Tracking System",
  "content": "## Plan\n\nBuild a complete Python GitHub repo with modular architecture. The system has clear module boundaries that allow parallel development after the initial project scaffold is set up.\n\n### Architecture\n- `models/` - Question bank data structures (Question, ProblemSet, StudentRecord)\n- `generators/` - Algorithmic question generators (arithmetic, algebra, MC)\n- `builder.py` - Problem-set builder that assembles sets from bank + generators\n- `grader.py` - Instant grading engine (numeric tolerance, MC matching)\n- `mastery.py` - 3-in-a-row difficulty bump + mastery tracking logic\n- `dashboard.py` - Simple CLI/text dashboard + report generation\n- `tests/` - Unit tests for all modules\n- `main.py` - CLI entry point tying it all together\n\n### Decomposition Strategy\n1. Scaffold the project structure and define core data models first (foundation)\n2. Build generators, grader, and mastery tracker in parallel (independent modules)\n3. Build the problem-set builder + dashboard (depends on models + generators)\n4. Integration: wire everything together with CLI entry point and tests\n\nUncertainty is low — requirements are clear. Work is decomposable → join=all.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "goal": "Create the project scaffold: directory structure (models/, generators/, tests/), pyproject.toml, README.md, and core data models in models/ — Question (with fields: id, text, answer, answer_type enum [numeric/mc], difficulty 1-5, topic, choices for MC), ProblemSet, StudentRecord (with history of attempts, streak tracking, current_difficulty, mastery_level per topic). Include __init__.py files and type hints throughout.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_claude_code_agent",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "goal": "Build the algorithmic question generators module (generators/). Implement: (1) ArithmeticGenerator - generates addition/subtraction/multiplication/division problems with difficulty-scaled operand ranges, (2) AlgebraGenerator - generates simple linear equation problems (solve for x) with difficulty scaling, (3) MCGenerator - wraps numeric generators to produce multiple-choice variants with plausible distractors. Each generator must conform to a Generator protocol/ABC that returns Question objects. Include a GeneratorRegistry that maps topic names to generators. Use the Question model schema: id (uuid), text (str), answer (str/float), answer_type ('numeric'|'mc'), difficulty (1-5), topic (str), choices (Optional[List[str]]).",
      "tool_name": "spawn_claude_code_agent",
      "depends_on": [0]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Build the grading engine (grader.py). Implement: (1) grade_numeric() - compares student answer to correct answer with configurable tolerance (default 0.01 for floats, exact for ints), returns GradeResult(correct: bool, student_answer, correct_answer, feedback: str), (2) grade_mc() - case-insensitive letter matching for multiple choice, (3) grade_question() - dispatcher that checks question.answer_type and routes to appropriate grader, (4) grade_problem_set() - grades a full set and returns ProblemSetResult with score, per-question results, and percentage. Use these model definitions: Question has answer_type in ['numeric', 'mc'], answer is stored as string.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_claude_code_agent",
      "depends_on": [0]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Build the mastery tracking module (mastery.py). Implement: (1) StreakTracker - tracks consecutive correct answers per topic per difficulty level, (2) 3-in-a-row difficulty bump logic: when a student gets 3 consecutive correct answers at difficulty N, auto-bump to difficulty N+1 (max 5), (3) MasteryTracker - maintains per-topic mastery state with levels [novice, beginner, intermediate, advanced, master] based on highest difficulty consistently passed (3-in-a-row at difficulty 5 = master), (4) record_attempt(topic, difficulty, correct) method that updates streak and mastery, (5) get_recommended_difficulty(topic) that returns current working difficulty, (6) streak resets to 0 on incorrect answer. Use StudentRecord schema with fields: topic_streaks (dict[str, int]), topic_difficulties (dict[str, int]), topic_mastery (dict[str, str]), attempt_history (list of dicts).",
      "tool_name": "spawn_claude_code_agent",
      "depends_on": [0]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Build the problem-set builder (builder.py) and the dashboard/report module (dashboard.py). For builder.py: (1) ProblemSetBuilder class that takes a GeneratorRegistry and MasteryTracker, (2) build_set(topics, num_questions, student_id) method that uses mastery tracker to determine difficulty per topic and generators to create questions, (3) supports mixed-topic sets with configurable topic weights. For dashboard.py: (1) print_problem_set() - formatted display of a problem set for the student, (2) print_grade_report() - shows score, per-question breakdown with ✓/✗, (3) print_mastery_dashboard() - shows per-topic mastery level, current difficulty, streak status in a formatted table, (4) generate_progress_report() - returns a markdown string summary of student progress across all topics. Use the Generator protocol, Question, ProblemSet, MasteryTracker, and GradeResult types from the other modules.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_claude_code_agent",
      "depends_on": [1, 2, 3]
    },
    {
      "goal": "Build the CLI entry point (main.py) and comprehensive tests (tests/). For main.py: implement an interactive CLI loop that (1) lets user pick topics, (2) generates a problem set via ProblemSetBuilder, (3) presents questions one at a time, (4) grades answers instantly with feedback, (5) updates mastery tracking with 3-in-a-row logic, (6) shows dashboard after each set. For tests/: write pytest tests covering (1) test_models.py - Question/ProblemSet creation and validation, (2) test_generators.py - each generator produces valid Questions at each difficulty, (3) test_grader.py - numeric tolerance, MC grading, edge cases, (4) test_mastery.py - streak tracking, 3-in-a-row bump, mastery level progression, streak reset on wrong answer, (5) test_builder.py - problem set assembly with correct difficulty routing, (6) test_integration.py - full flow from generation through grading to mastery update. Also add a complete README.md with usage instructions, architecture overview, and examples.",
      "tool_name": "spawn_claude_code_agent",
      "depends_on": [4]
    }
  ],
